/P 305 0 R
/E (Meanwhile, crop-residue burning remains a serious concern: for example, in Delhi the contribution of stubble burning to PM2.5 pollution reached over 30 % at times during the late 2024 season. In Punjab, ex-situ management of over 6.2 million tonnes of paddy straw in 2024 helped reduce fire incidents by around 70 % in that state alone.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
647 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 305 0 R
/E (These interconnected challenges, soil deterioration, inefficient mechanisation, environmentally harmful post-harvest practices and exposure to climate risk, place millions of small and marginal farmers at risk of declining incomes and unsustainable livelihoods. At the same time, they affect water security, air quality and ecosystem health. This is why sustainable agriculture is not just about increasing yields, it is about restoring balance among people, planet and production; enabling farmers to thrive economically while preserving the natural capital they depend on.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
