/Title (Project Sahyog is a large-scale farm mechanisation and knowledge-transfer initiative implemented across Haryana, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, and Uttarakhand. The program equips farmers with Tractor-Mounted and Self-Propelled Boom Sprayers \(TMS & SPBS\), promotes the judicious use of agrochemicals, and fosters entrepreneurship by enabling beneficiaries to rent out equipment to their peers. Through a blend of training, demonstrations, and IEC campaigns, the project strengthens farm productivity, reduces input costs, and creates sustainable income streams for rural communities)
