7087 0 obj
<<
/Title (Pushpa Kumari: A Catalyst for Change Pushpa Kumari, a smallholder farmer from Dadi village, struggled with declining yields and high fertiliser costs. After attending Harit Samriddhi training, she adopted crop rotation and integrated pest management. Within a single season, her soil health improved, fertiliser use dropped by 25%, and yields rose noticeably. Seeing her success, five other women farmers in the village adopted similar practices, collectively covering 15 acres under improved methods. Pushpa now leads farmer meetings as a peer educator, symbolising the ripple effect of knowledge-sharing that Project Harit Samriddhi aims to create.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
