<<
/Title (Sports for All is a CSR initiative supported by Honda India Foundation and implemented by Roots Foundation in partnership with Smile Foundation. Launched in May 2024, the program provides structured physical fitness and sports training in government schools, with the vision that every child, regardless of socio-economic background, deserves access to quality sports opportunities. The program currently operates in three schools: Primary School Pali \(Greater Noida\), Government Girls Senior Secondary School \(Tapukara, Rajasthan\), and Government Senior Secondary School \(Budhi Bawal, Rajasthan\). With three dedicated coaches working six days a week, the initiative integrates daily PE classes, evening sports camps, career counselling, and exposure to tournaments, creating an inclusive ecosystem where students can thrive.)
